{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789219510,"nonce":"y1opmisUIn4CuQM3OXMBA42+9MM=","title":"a Dynamic holding an Array cannot be read: `d.length`, `d.hasNext`, Reflect.field on it crash; haxe.Template `::foreach::` dies there","message":"Reproducer (crashes at HEAD and at the fix commits alike):\n\n    static function get():Dynamic return [1, 2];\n    var v:Dynamic = get();\n    v.length;                       // SIGSEGV fault=0x2\n    Reflect.field(v, \"hasNext\");    // SIGSEGV fault=0xb5\n\n`var v:Dynamic = [1, 2]; v.hasNext == null` in the same function is fine, so\nthe value's representation differs by producer. An array boxed for Dynamic\ngets `haxe_box_reference_ptr(arr, \u003craw TAST TypeId\u003e)`: `runtime_type_id`\n(mir/helpers/type_ids.rs) has no Array arm, so the runtime's TYPE_ARRAY (7)\nis never used and no reader can tell an array box from anything else. The\ndynamic field read then does `haxe_unbox_reference_ptr` + `haxe_reflect_field`\non the array pointer as if it were a class object.\n\nConsequences:\n- haxe.Template `::foreach::` (Issue5293, Issue9372): `v.iterator()` on the\n  Dynamic now throws the E0801 message at runtime (the compile error was\n  turned into a throw so the rest of the module compiles); the catch path's\n  `v.hasNext` then crashes as above. Both rows were WRONG_ANSWER while\n  Template returned \"\" for every input; they are CRASH now.\n- `Std.isOfType(d, Array)` compares against fnv(\"Array\"), which no box carries.\n\nFix direction: box arrays with TYPE_ARRAY and give the `Array` class symbol\nthe same id; make dynamic field reads consult the box tag before unboxing\n(length / hasNext / iterator on an array box); then the ambiguous dynamic\ndispatch in stdlib_instance.rs can switch on the tag among its candidates\ninstead of throwing.","files":null}]}